    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0901" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg859"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 406</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">752.11/7–1151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Maddox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d406-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-07-11T13:00:00+01:00">July 11, 1951—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Deptel 15, July 10; Madrid 45 June
                        23.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d406-f2"/> In conversation with Xanthaky<anchor n="3" xml:id="d406-f3"/> last
                    night, Spanish pretender flatly denied story that Spanish Amb Nicolas Franco, or any other representative of
                    Caudillo, has proposed to him that he renounce rights in favor of his son.</p>
                <pb facs="0902" n="860" xml:id="pg860"/>
                <p>According to pretender following is genesis stories circulating Madrid: Last
                    month Franco apparently remarked at close
                    of Cabinet, members (Don Juan specifically
                    mentioned Artajo, Giron and
                        Fernandez Cuesta) launched trial balloon at latter’s
                    social gathering by insinuating story in question. “Although,” says pretender,
                    “this would be facile solution from Franco viewpoint, they obviously would not have temerity to make
                    such proposal to me as they know full well its rejection would be foregone
                    conclusion”. In Don Juan’s opinion,
                    therefore, July 18 will come to pass without, as rumored, Franco indicating his successor.</p>
                <p>Pretender has also heard that Dr. Duarte, Franco’s physician, wishes Caudillo to undergo
                    gallstone operation and that operating room actually being installed in Pardo,
                    but matter not urgent and Franco still
                    undecided. Concerning rumors structural changes in Spanish Govt, pretender
                    discounts these entirely stating not in Franco’s nature delegate power and furthermore that when former
                    Cabinet Minister Larraz recently made such suggestion to Franco, latter promptly changed subject.
                    Pretender inclined believe Franco now
                    banking very heavily on mil and econ aid from US to bolster his prestige and if
                    this should be forthcoming he will continue stalling tactics and postpone
                    practical consideration matter of succession indefinitely.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Maddox</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
